==========================================================================
1. WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS
==========================================================================

"PeterShip" means the shipping client described in this folder and its
source code, wherever it lives in this repository, including:

   - everything under shipping-client/
   - everything under site/src/shipping/ (the rating engine, billable
     weight rules, HTTP and OAuth helpers, the carrier adapters for USPS,
     UPS, FedEx, DHL Express and Easyship, and their types)
   - the shipping, label, tracking and reconciliation tables in
     site/db/schema.sql
   - the carrier configuration keys in site/.dev.vars.example and
     site/wrangler.jsonc
   - any later file that the Owners mark as part of PeterShip, and any
     documentation, design or test written for the above

PeterShip is NOT covered by the Apache License, Version 2.0 or the
Creative Commons license in the repository root LICENSE file. Where that
file and this one conflict about a PeterShip file, this file controls.

The rest of the repository keeps its root LICENSE and NOTICE.

==========================================================================
2. WHAT YOU MAY DO
==========================================================================

You may:

   a. Read the PeterShip source code, and study how it works.
   b. Run it on your own machine for the purpose of evaluating it or
      proposing changes to the Owners.
   c. Copy short excerpts (under fifty lines) into a bug report, question
      or review about PeterShip.

You do not need permission for the uses above, and you may not charge
anyone for them.

==========================================================================
3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
==========================================================================

Unless you have a signed, written license from all of the Owners, you
may not:

   a. Use PeterShip, or any part of it, to run a shipping, mailbox,
      printing, packing, fulfillment or logistics business, or to quote,
      sell or print shipping labels for anyone, other than the Owners'
      own store.
   b. Deploy PeterShip to any server, Cloudflare account or other hosting
      that the Owners do not control.
   c. Sell, rent, lease, sublicense, lend or otherwise distribute
      PeterShip or any part of it, whether as source, object code or a
      hosted service.
   d. Create, distribute or run a derivative work of PeterShip, including
      a port to another language, platform or carrier.
   e. Use PeterShip to build or train a competing product, or offer it,
      or a product based on it, to another Goin' Postal franchisee or to
      any other shipping store.
   f. Remove or change any copyright, license or attribution notice in
      PeterShip.
   g. Use the name "PeterShip" for any product or service.

